            "prompt": "You are an ESL teacher designing a set of cards to teach the meaning of words.\n\n* Create a one dimensional array of pipe delimited strings (sentences), of the following pattern: keyword|keyword-translation|keyword-examplesentence| keyword-examplesentence-translation\nThe keywords to use are contained in this list: [{keywords}].  \nThe translation language is: {nativelanguage}. The keyword and example sentence language is: {targetlanguage}\n\n* Create a second one dimensional array (data2) that contains just the keyword|keyword-translation \n\n* Also create a matching one-dimensional array of image generation prompts (data1) to illustrate each keyword in the context of the example sentence. Determine the image prompt generation style based on the keyword type: For Concrete Words (Nouns, Objects, Animals): Keep the image prompt straightforward. Focus on a clear, high-quality depiction of the object or action described in the sentence. For Abstract Words, Quantifiers, or Concepts (e.g., most, fast, carefully, freedom): Do not just draw a generic scene of the sentence. Instead, design the composition to highlight the meaning of the word itself. Use visual contrast, clear proportions (e.g., a massive group vs. a tiny group for \"most\"), or a strong focus on the specific action to make the abstract concept immediately recognizable at a glance.",
